  "coverageInterpretation": [
    "139788 input rows minus 138 duplicate epochs leave 139650 actual anchors; each horizon partitions all admitted anchors into accepted pairs or explicit exclusions.",
    "68339 of 139650 buffered truth rows are accepted primary comparisons. This measures row eligibility and reference coverage, not a time-based playback success rate.",
    "30257 buffered truth rows were already delivered, 2434 carry stale-position flags, and 88 have no available model. Available held-out comparisons, including expired/excluded positions, remain separately reported.",
    "The one-second clock grid has 2547048 slots, 234733 with a non-stale recorded fix within one second, and 2312315 without reference truth. These missing slots are not scored using invented positions.",
    "Each trace begins without earlier truth for its initial 25-second presentation buffer; 2525 aggregate seconds across 101 traces are counted separately.",
    "Primary quantiles are conditional on eligibility and boundary rules. Pre-exclusion maxima include frozen expired positions across long source gaps; they are not accepted fresh estimates."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "One date, one staging release, first complete files from its first 4MiB, all identifiers suffix e3: archive-order convenience sample, not random or representative global validation.",
    "Buffered delivery is simulated every 30 seconds. Only fixes recorded by each delivery epoch are admitted; actual fix epochs are never retimed and intermediate truth remains withheld.",
    "No interpolated or fabricated truth fills missing positions. Archived recording is denser than live acquisition and does not establish live delivery, dropouts, request age or rendering performance.",
    "Offline boundary labels can use withheld source truth to exclude primary comparisons; the model cannot see those labels. Unfiltered available errors preserve the impact of exclusions.",
    "Correction blending is disabled for these math comparisons and needs independent browser proof. The chosen UI fixture does not filter bulk calibration.",
    "Quantiles are measurements on correlated fixes, not calibrated confidence or an accuracy guarantee. Raw traces, coordinates and observation sequences are omitted."
  ]
